{
  "as_of": "2026-09-28",
  "scope": "Strict HTTP URI-reference metadata in request Content-Location and interim/final response Location and Content-Location, through Go/Python request admission, direct Go transport, parsed/wire response checks and complete-body delivery.",
  "changes": [
    "Shared Go URI-reference grammar checks scheme, authority, IPv6/IPvFuture literals, port characters, path/query/fragment alphabets and percent escapes without repair or decoding. Python enforces the same contract.",
    "Content-Location excludes fragments. Explicit HTTP(S) and inherited network-path references require a nonempty host and forbid userinfo. Generic non-HTTP schemes remain metadata and receive generic URI grammar only.",
    "Request grammar and duplicate/empty-array checks run before inspection or DNS. Responses are checked in raw interim/final header blocks, parsed metadata and the Go complete-body backstop, including custom MCP response delivery.",
    "Accepted URI spelling is retained; it cannot change the destination, trigger a fetch or expand origin authorization. MIME part URI metadata retains its separate grammar/encoding contract.",
    "No Snort SID, deployed network route or sandbox boundary changed."
  ],
